-- title:
--   Frobenius pairing on a finite power-series quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $n$ a natural number, and write $R = k[[X_0,\dots,X_{n-1}]]$ for the ring `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k`. Let $g$ be an $n \times n$ matrix with entries in $R$ and let $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to R$ be a family of power series such that $f_i = \sum_j g_{ij} X_j$ for every $i$, i.e. $f = g \cdot X$ where $X$ is the column of the variables. Put $A = R / (f_0,\dots,f_{n-1})$, the quotient of $R$ by the ideal generated by the range of $f$, and assume that $A$ is finite-dimensional as a $k$-module. Then there exists a $k$-linear functional $l : A \to k$ such that the $k$-linear map $A \to \mathrm{Hom}_k(A,k)$ sending $a$ to the functional $b \mapsto l(ab)$ — the multiplication bilinear map `LinearMap.mul k A` composed on the right with $l$, written `(LinearMap.mul k A).compr₂ l` — is bijective. Equivalently, the symmetric bilinear form $(a,b) \mapsto l(ab)$ on $A$ is perfect, so $A$ is a Frobenius $k$-algebra.
--
--   This is the statement that a finite-dimensional quotient of a power-series ring by $n$ relations of the shape $f = g\cdot X$ is a Frobenius (Gorenstein Artinian) $k$-algebra, in the form of the existence of a trace-like functional with perfect multiplication pairing. It is used in the construction of pairings on complete intersections over a field: it feeds [`Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_isAlgClosed) and [`Algebra.exists_pairing_of_exists_presentation`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_pairing_of_exists_presentation).
